			}]
			title: "The Sea's Temple"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["73837610E788A3CD"]
			description: ["Acropolis floats high above the open sea, its citizens evolved to live without the water, yet still forever attached to it. At its pinnacle sits &6&oScylla, The Storm Empress&r. In your search for power and the Legendary Eyes, you will need to conquer this floating city."]
			id: "36BF42D396F66FE3"
			tasks: [{
				icon: "cataclysm:storm_eye"
				id: "7ED9EEF586EB5742"
				structure: "cataclysm:acropolis"
				title: "Find Acropolis"
				type: "structure"
			}]
			title: "A Sanctuary Of Storms"
			x: -2.5d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["36BF42D396F66FE3"]
			description: [
				"To combat The Storm Empress, one must simply find her anchor at the peak of Acropolis. But be prepared, as &6&oher heavy strikes and ability with electrocution&r will live up to her title."
				"Scylla's anchor is her primary weapon, capable of grabbing foes from afar. She can also send out torrents of water, &6&omaking her enemy wet and amplifying her electrical attacks&r, such as a spear of lightning that bypasses armor."
				"To fight one such as her is never an even match, magical serpents being summoned to aid Scylla in your defeat."
				"&6&oIndeed, be aware of the water, be careful of the anchor, and you may yet live to see another day.&r"
			]
			id: "52DACA3870E942B9"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "cataclysm:scylla"
				icon: "cataclysm:ceraunus"
				id: "653013C5B6F2124F"
				title: "Slay Scylla, the Storm Empress"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "Storm's End"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["73837610E788A3CD"]
			description: ["An ancient civilization that still thrives, Deeplings inhabit what can only be called the Sunken City. A gargantuan structure found in Deep Oceans and completely submerged in water, it houses the brother of Scylla, &o&6The Leviathan&r. If you wish to lay claim to The Legendary Eyes, this will be one of your key destinations. Best not make it your last."]
			id: "24D211740DD41A5D"
			tasks: [{
				icon: "cataclysm:abyss_eye"
				id: "5F1CBCECBA22795D"
				structure: "cataclysm:sunken_city"
				title: "Find The Sunken City"
				type: "structure"
			}]
			title: "The Abyss Calls Back"
			x: -2.5d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["24D211740DD41A5D"]
			description: [
				"To summon The Leviathan is by no means an easy task. It will require an Abyssal Sacrifice, crafted using &o&6rare materials and items plucked from the bodies of the city's residents&r. Of all the ingredients, the two that stand out are &6&oThe Athame and Coral Chunk&r."
				"The Athame is a holy dagger held only by Deepling Priests and Warlocks, used in abyssal rituals. Coral chunks can be ripped off of a dead Coralssus, akin to golems and powerful mounts."
			]
			id: "4EB7EBA9F1F56744"
			tasks: [{
				id: "583000F692AA7095"
				item: "cataclysm:abyssal_sacrifice"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Sacrificial Blessings"
			x: -1.5d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4EB7EBA9F1F56744"]
			description: [
				"To kill The Leviathan is to combat the Abyss itself. You would best prepare yourself for combat in the water, and carry with you Blessed Amethyst Crab Meat, gained by &6&oslaying an Amethyst Crab in Lush Caves and blessing its meat at the Sunken City's Amethyst Altar&r."
				"Knowledge of one's surroundings is key in this battle, as The Leviathan's maw and tentacles will strike as you avoid making contact with the Abyssal Mines floating throughout the arena. &6&oDodge its strikes, projectiles, and mines, and victory may be yours.&r"
			]
			id: "01994F72AF7D412B"
			tasks: [{
				entity: "cataclysm:the_leviathan"
				icon: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbquests:custom_icon"
					tag: {
						Icon: "cataclysm:textures/mob_effect/abyssal_curse.png"
					}
				}
				id: "151B885D954CEC82"
				title: "Kill The Leviathan"
				type: "kill"
				value: 1L
			}]
			title: "Silence Once More"
			x: -0.5d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["69BEEF688AA76D82"]
			description: [
				"Exploring the vast ocean is a long an arduous journey. It's for this reason that a proper ship becomes a necessity. Whether it be a Cog for simple traversal, particularly in cold waters, a Brigg for transportation of many items and passengers, a Galley for naval warfare, or a Drakkar for the true Norse experience."
				"All ships have their uses, and all use the sails, let down with the necessary keybind (Default R). From there, speed is increased with W and decreased with S."
				"For some extra personality, you can dye the sails of your ship."
			]
			id: "2270E70D4E4E6E86"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5413FED76BD2EA68"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "itemfilters:tag"
